"""Continuous-action Relative-Q: CW-Pair and CW-Duel critics on a DDPG or TD3 base (2026-11-04).

Entry points (one file per base, all logic here):  stoix/systems/ddpg/ff_cw_ddpg.py, stoix/systems/ddpg/ff_cw_td3.py
  system.head = q     plain Q critic = the base algorithm itself (baseline; same pipeline, same truncation handling)
              = pair  CW-Pair: free pair head D(x, y), x = (s, a)
              = duel  CW-Duel: D((s,a),(t,b)) = W(s,t) + A(s,a) - A(t,b)
              = qcw   CW-Q (2026-11-04): D(x, y) = Q(x) - Q(y) with the plain unary critic Q(s,a); all-pairs /
                      rho weight matrix as duel; TD3 next value min_k Q_k^-(s',a~); actor = TD3 actor. No scalar c.
  system.pairing = rho     same-trajectory groups + cross-group pairs, weight (1-rho) / rho  (system.pair_rho, st_group)
                 = random  i.i.d. batch: pair head K cyclic shifts, duel head all off-diagonal pairs (uniform)

Networks (flat observation vector s, action a in [a_min, a_max]^n; all hidden layers silu):
  QCritic     Q(s,a) = Dense1(MLP(q_hidden)([s, a]))
  PairCritic  h = MLP(torso)(s);  e(s,a) = MLP(enc)([h, a]);  D(x,y) = Dense1(MLP(pair_hidden)([e_x, e_y]))
  DuelCritic  h = MLP(torso)(s);  W(s,t) = w(s) - w(t) + z1(s).z2(t) - z2(s).z1(t)   (antisymmetric, rank r)
              f(s,a) = Dense1(MLP(f_hidden)([h, a]));  A(s,a) = f(s,a) - f(s, a_ref(s)),  a_ref(s) = mu^-(s)
              (target actor, no noise, no gradient) -> A(s, mu^-(s)) = 0: the continuous analogue of the max-centred
              advantage of the discrete Dueling/CW-Duel stream; the state value is carried by W.

Bootstrap (target networks; a~_x = mu^-(s'_x) (+ clipped Gaussian noise for TD3, target policy smoothing)):
  M = D^-((s'_x,a~_x),(s'_y,a~_y)),  Amax = D^-((s'_x,a~_x), y),  Bmin = D^-(x, (s'_y,a~_y))
  current-state parts (the y in Amax, the x in Bmin) from the TARGET critic (the online-sg variant diverged, 11-02).
  Cross-weighted residual (same formula as the discrete CW-Pair, ff_rpair.py), G = g(1-d), v = 1-G, k = (1-g)/g:
    xi = v_y r_x - v_x r_y + kG_xG_y M + G_x(v_y - kG_y) Amax + G_y(v_x - kG_x) Bmin + (-v_y - G_y(v_x - kG_x)) D(x,y)
  target T = sg[D + xi/(1-g)],  critic loss 0.5 sum_pairs w (T - D)^2   (sum w = 1).
  d = TRUE termination only (system.truncation_bootstrap=True): time-limit truncation is bootstrapped (DMC ends every
  episode by truncation at 1000 steps).  Trajectory boundaries for same-trajectory pairing use the episode-end flag
  (info.is_terminal_step, termination OR truncation).

Actor (deterministic, tanh-scaled; maximise the critic's read-out of the actor action):
  q    : -mean Q_1(s, mu(s))
  pair : -sum_pairs w D_1((s_x, mu(s_x)), sg[y])      (anchor read-out on the training pairs, x role)
  duel : -mean f_1(s, mu(s))                          (= -mean A_1(s, mu(s)) up to an actor-independent term)

TD3 (base='td3'): twin critics, target policy smoothing (policy_noise, noise_clip), delayed actor update
(policy_frequency, via optax.conditionally_mask as in Stoix ff_td3).  Clipped double estimate:
  q    : min_k Q_k^-(s', a~)                                            (standard)
  pair : both critics regress to min_k T_k(x,y)      (pessimistic in the x role, which is the role the actor reads)
  duel : the next-state advantage A^-(s',a~) is min_k A_k^-(s',a~) inside each critic's own target (W_k own);
         a min over the whole antisymmetric pair target would cancel between (i,j) and (j,i).
DDPG (base='ddpg'): one critic, no smoothing, actor every step.
"""
